{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nArkady wants to have a dinner. He has just returned from a shop where he has bought a semifinished cutlet. He only needs to fry it. The cutlet should be fried for 2n seconds, in particular, it should be fried for n seconds on one side and n seconds on the other side. Arkady has already got a frying pan and turn on fire, but understood that maybe he won't be able to flip the cutlet exactly after n seconds after the beginning of cooking.Arkady is too busy with sorting sticker packs in his favorite messenger and can flip the cutlet only in some periods of time. Namely, there are k periods of time in which he can do it, the i-th of them is an interval of time from li seconds after he starts cooking till ri seconds, inclusive. Arkady decided that it's not required to flip the cutlet exactly in the middle of cooking, instead, he will flip it several times in such a way that the cutlet will be fried exactly n seconds on one side and n seconds on the other side in total.Help Arkady and find out if it's possible for him to cook the cutlet, if he is able to flip the cutlet only in given periods of time; and if yes, find the minimum number of flips he needs to cook the cutlet.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class CF939F_V2 {\n    static final int INF = (int) 1e8;\n    static BufferedReader input;\n    static PrintWriter output;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        if (System.getProperty(\"ONLINE_JUDGE\") == null) {\n            input = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(\"D:\\\\DataBase\\\\TESTCASE\\\\codeforces\\\\CF939F.in\"));\n        } else {\n            input = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n        output = new PrintWriter(new BufferedOutputStream(System.out));\n        \n        solve();\n        output.flush();\n    }\n\n    static void solve() throws IOException {\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(input.readLine().trim());\n        int k = Integer.parseInt(input.readLine().trim());\n        \n        int[][] intervals = new int[k + 2][2];\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n            String[] parts = input.readLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            intervals[i][0] = Integer.parseInt(parts[0]);\n            intervals[i][1] = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);\n        }\n        intervals[k + 1][0] = 2 * n;\n        intervals[k + 1][1] = 2 * n;\n        k++;\n\n        int[][] dp = new int[2][n + 1];\n        Arrays.fill(dp[0], INF);\n        dp[0][0] = 0;\n\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n            int cur = i & 1;\n            int prev = (i - 1) & 1;\n            Arrays.fill(dp[cur], INF);\n\n            int[] interval = intervals[i];\n            int intervalLength = interval[1] - interval[0];\n            int middleLength = interval[0] - intervals[i - 1][1];\n\n            for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) {\n                if (j >= intervalLength + middleLength) {\n                    dp[cur][j] = dp[prev][j - intervalLength - middleLength];\n                }\n            }\n\n            int minX = interval[1] - middleLength - intervalLength;\n            int maxX = interval[1] - middleLength;\n            for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) {\n                int minNeedTime = INF;\n                for (int x = Math.max(0, minX - j); x <= Math.min(n, maxX - j); x++) {\n                    minNeedTime = Math.min(minNeedTime, dp[prev][x]);\n                }\n                dp[cur][j] = Math.min(dp[cur][j], minNeedTime + 1);\n            }\n\n            for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) {\n                int minNeedTime = INF;\n                for (int x = interval[1] - intervalLength; x <= interval[1]; x++) {\n                    minNeedTime = Math.min(minNeedTime, dp[prev][x]);\n                }\n                dp[cur][j] = Math.min(dp[cur][j], minNeedTime + 2);\n            }\n        }\n\n        int minFlipTime = dp[k & 1][n];\n\n        if (minFlipTime < INF) {\n            output.println(\"Full\");\n            output.println(minFlipTime);\n        } else {\n            output.println(\"Hungry\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class CF939F_V2 {\n    static final int INF = (int) 1e8;\n    static BufferedReader input;\n    static PrintWriter output;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        if (System.getProperty(\"ONLINE_JUDGE\") == null) {\n            input = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(\"D:\\\\DataBase\\\\TESTCASE\\\\codeforces\\\\CF939F.in\"));\n        } else {\n            input = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n        output = new PrintWriter(new BufferedOutputStream(System.out));\n        \n        solve();\n        output.flush();\n    }\n\n    static void solve() throws IOException {\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(input.readLine().trim());\n        int k = Integer.parseInt(input.readLine().trim());\n        \n        int[][] intervals = new int[k + 2][2];\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n            String[] parts = input.readLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            intervals[i][0] = Integer.parseInt(parts[0]);\n            intervals[i][1] = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);\n        }\n        intervals[k + 1][0] = 2 * n;\n        intervals[k + 1][1] = 2 * n;\n        k++;\n\n        // dp[i][j] = minimum flips to have j seconds on the first side after processing first i intervals\n        int[][] dp = new int[k + 1][n + 1];\n        for (int i = 0; i <= k; i++) {\n            Arrays.fill(dp[i], INF);\n        }\n        dp[0][0] = 0;\n\n        int prevEnd = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n            int start = intervals[i][0];\n            int end = intervals[i][1];\n            \n            // Copy previous state\n            for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) {\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j];\n            }\n            \n            // Time available in current interval\n            int intervalLen = end - start + 1;\n            \n            // Try all possible ways to use the current interval\n            for (int prevSide = 0; prevSide <= n; prevSide++) {\n                if (dp[i-1][prevSide] == INF) continue;\n                \n                // Try 0 flips in this interval\n                int timeOnPrevSide = Math.min(intervalLen, Math.max(0, end - prevEnd));\n                if (prevSide + timeOnPrevSide <= n) {\n                    dp[i][prevSide + timeOnPrevSide] = Math.min(dp[i][prevSide + timeOnPrevSide], dp[i-1][prevSide]);\n                }\n                \n                // Try 1 flip in this interval\n                for (int flipTime = start; flipTime <= end; flipTime++) {\n                    int timeOnPrevSide1 = flipTime - prevEnd;\n                    int timeOnOtherSide = end - flipTime + 1;\n                    \n                    if (timeOnPrevSide1 >= 0 && prevSide + timeOnPrevSide1 <= n) {\n                        int newSide = prevSide + timeOnPrevSide1;\n                        if (newSide + timeOnOtherSide <= n) {\n                            dp[i][newSide + timeOnOtherSide] = Math.min(dp[i][newSide + timeOnOtherSide], dp[i-1][prevSide] + 1);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                \n                // Try 2 flips in this interval (flip in and flip out)\n                for (int flipIn = start; flipIn <= end; flipIn++) {\n                    for (int flipOut = flipIn; flipOut <= end; flipOut++) {\n                        int timeOnPrevSide1 = flipIn - prevEnd;\n                        int timeOnOtherSide = flipOut - flipIn;\n                        int timeOnPrevSide2 = end - flipOut + 1;\n                        \n                        if (timeOnPrevSide1 >= 0 && prevSide + timeOnPrevSide1 <= n) {\n                            int newSide = prevSide + timeOnPrevSide1;\n                            if (newSide + timeOnOtherSide <= n) {\n                                int finalSide = newSide + timeOnOtherSide + timeOnPrevSide2;\n                                if (finalSide <= n) {\n                                    dp[i][finalSide] = Math.min(dp[i][finalSide], dp[i-1][prevSide] + 2);\n                                }\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            \n            prevEnd = end;\n        }\n\n        if (dp[k][n] < INF) {\n            output.println(\"Full\");\n            output.println(dp[k][n]);\n        } else {\n            output.println(\"Hungry\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.364403477869928e-06, -0.0001212284987559542, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.663577369181439e-05, -1.966933996300213e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -8.583032467868179e